---
name: lite-dev-task
version: 1.0.0
description: Dev assignment for a lite-profile bead.
format: xml
required_variables: [provider, task_id, sprint, phase, worktree_path, branch, pr_target, lint_command, test_command]
metadata:
  type: dev-task
  tags: [stage:dev, orchestration:beads, profile:lite]
  workflow:
    scope: {kind: sprint, variable: sprint}
    state: dev-start
    stage: dev
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" profile="lite">
  <description><![CDATA[Implement the assigned lite bead. Its description, design, acceptance criteria, and owned_paths are authoritative.]]></description>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch }}]]></branch>
  <pr-target><![CDATA[{{ pr_target }}]]></pr-target>
  <workflow>
    <step><![CDATA[Run assignment gates and claim/start the bead. Read its full scope and stay within owned_paths.]]></step>
    <step><![CDATA[Implement and validate with {{ test_command }} and {{ lint_command }}. Keep every test deterministic; do not use timing, sleeps, races, or event-loop ordering.]]></step>
    <step><![CDATA[Push the branch and open/update its PR against the current stack top. Record the exact stack view and evidence.]]></step>
    <step><![CDATA[Complete with .atm-bd/scripts/hook_runner.py --role dev --phase {{ phase }} --vars <lead-vars> --result <result.json>. The installed runner gathers live bead, task, PR, and stack state before planning or running the transition.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
